  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hatrick**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [4]\n- **banter - inviting out Christian Scott**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - update on solo projects**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **What You See**: back after 94 archived shows (2022 days); rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **banter - inviting out Nigel Hall**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - bringing back John Scofield & Christian Scott**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **thanks/announcements**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2009-07-31** (recommended): audience recording; 16 songs; 106 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **soulive2009-07-31.flac24**: audience recording; 16 songs; 106 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: banter - Scofield [1]\n- The show was part of the 2009 Celebrate Brooklyn Festival, with Ivan Neville's Dumpstaphunk opening the night [1]\n- Guests marked in the notes: Christian Scott on trumpet, John Scofield on guitar, Nigel Hall on vocals, plus Ivan Neville and Tony Hall on vocals [1]\n- Part of the 2009 Celebrate Brooklyn Festival; Dumpstaphunk opened, and the uploader also taped their set [2]\n- Guests marked: Christian Scott on trumpet, John Scofield on guitar, Nigel Hall on vocals, Ivan Neville and Tony Hall on vocals [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2009-07-31**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [1]. Also: Scott Bernstein recorded, mastered and tracked this recording; a higher quality 24 bit version is also available [1]\n- **soulive2009-07-31.flac24**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [2]. Also: Scott Bernstein recorded, mastered and tracked this 24 bit fileset, which is not meant for CD burning, streaming or MP3s [2]",
